    {
      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nvoid read_dataset(int *nbodies, float **px, float **py, float **pz,\n                  float **vx, float **vy, float **vz) {\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) { fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading nbodie value\\n\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n  int n = *nbodies;\n  Body *tmp = (Body *)malloc(n * sizeof(Body));\n  b = fread(tmp, n * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n  if (b != 1) { fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError reading input values\\n\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n  *px = (float*)malloc(n*sizeof(float));\n  *py = (float*)malloc(n*sizeof(float));\n  *pz = (float*)malloc(n*sizeof(float));\n  *vx = (float*)malloc(n*sizeof(float));\n  *vy = (float*)malloc(n*sizeof(float));\n  *vz = (float*)malloc(n*sizeof(float));\n  for (int i=0;i<n;i++){\n    (*px)[i] = tmp[i].x;\n    (*py)[i] = tmp[i].y;\n    (*pz)[i] = tmp[i].z;\n    (*vx)[i] = tmp[i].vx;\n    (*vy)[i] = tmp[i].vy;\n    (*vz)[i] = tmp[i].vz;\n  }\n  free(tmp);\n}\n\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, float *px, float *py, float *pz,\n                   float *vx, float *vy, float *vz) {\n  Body *out = (Body*)malloc(nbodies*sizeof(Body));\n  for (int i=0;i<nbodies;i++){\n    out[i].x = px[i];\n    out[i].y = py[i];\n    out[i].z = pz[i];\n    out[i].vx = vx[i];\n    out[i].vy = vy[i];\n    out[i].vz = vz[i];\n  }\n  int b = fwrite(out, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n  if (b != 1) { fprintf(stderr,\"\\nError writing to output\\n\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n  free(out);\n}\n\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\n  int nbodies;\n  float *px,*py,*pz,*vx,*vy,*vz;\n  read_dataset(&nbodies,&px,&py,&pz,&vx,&vy,&vz);\n\n  const int TILE = 64;\n\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n    #pragma omp parallel\n    {\n      // Force computation: dynamic scheduling on tiles balances load.\n      #pragma omp for schedule(dynamic,16)\n      for (int i0 = 0; i0 < nbodies; i0 += TILE) {\n        int i_end = i0 + TILE;\n        if (i_end > nbodies) i_end = nbodies;\n        int cnt = i_end - i0;\n\n        float fx[64], fy[64], fz[64];\n        float xis[64], yis[64], zis[64];\n\n        for (int t = 0; t < cnt; ++t) {\n          fx[t] = 0.0f;\n          fy[t] = 0.0f;\n          fz[t] = 0.0f;\n          int idx = i0 + t;\n          xis[t] = px[idx];\n          yis[t] = py[idx];\n          zis[t] = pz[idx];\n        }\n\n#define ACCUM(jj) \\\n    do { \\\n      float pjx = px[jj]; \\\n      float pjy = py[jj]; \\\n      float pjz = pz[jj]; \\\n      _Pragma(\"omp simd\") \\\n      for (int t = 0; t < cnt; ++t) { \\\n        float dx = pjx - xis[t]; \\\n        float dy = pjy - yis[t]; \\\n        float dz = pjz - zis[t]; \\\n        float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING; \\\n        float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist); \\\n        float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist; \\\n        fx[t] += dx * inv_dist3; \\\n        fy[t] += dy * inv_dist3; \\\n        fz[t] += dz * inv_dist3; \\\n      } \\\n    } while (0)\n\n        int j = 0;\n        for (; j + 3 < nbodies; j += 4) {\n          ACCUM(j);\n          ACCUM(j+1);\n          ACCUM(j+2);\n          ACCUM(j+3);\n        }\n        for (; j < nbodies; ++j) {\n          ACCUM(j);\n        }\n#undef ACCUM\n\n        // Update velocities within this tile.\n        for (int t = 0; t < cnt; ++t) {\n          int idx = i0 + t;\n          vx[idx] += DT * fx[t];\n          vy[idx] += DT * fy[t];\n          vz[idx] += DT * fz[t];\n        }\n      }\n\n      // Position update: static schedule.\n      #pragma omp for schedule(static)\n      for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        px[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n        py[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n        pz[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  write_dataset(nbodies, px, py, pz, vx, vy, vz);\n\n  free(px); free(py); free(pz);\n  free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining SoA layout, restrict pointers, tiled force computation with unrolled inner loop and omp simd accumulation, hoisted per-tile positions, dynamic scheduling on tiles, and inlined body_force into a single OpenMP parallel region will yield better speedup than any individual transformation.",
  "notes": "The implementation preserves exact floating-point summation order per body: the j-loop is unrolled by 4 but each ACCUM call processes contributions sequentially for every i within a tile. The omp simd pragma vectorizes across independent i values without changing per-i reduction order. Dynamic scheduling on tiles balances load while static scheduling handles the trivial position update.",
